From 2f9bd5b4d42050478d68ae62dae28af4a7003e9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:47:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(motion): rework Bore pass start onto the shared
 warning law

Merge origin/main (e313aa663, the #3353 merge) into the branch.

Blocker 1: the merged main removed PassStart::rank, so bore.rs no longer
compiled (E0599). Order the bore rings directly from PassStart: Auto and
Inside keep the centre-out walk, and Outside reverses it to cut the wall
ring first. Auto stays byte-for-byte identical.

Blocker 2: bore Outside cuts the wall ring at the full tool width. The
family warning law of #3402 (#3316) needs a note for it. bore_started now
adds StartSide::wall_first_note() to the path notes for Outside, and posts
none for Auto and Inside. The note does not change the moves.

Pinned by bore_outside_names_the_full_width_wall_cut.

Refs #3360

